cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "benchLANG: Reproducible Programming Language Performance Benchmark"
message: "If you use these results, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gleb
    family-names: Olsen
repository-code: "https://github.com/glebolsen/benchLANG"
abstract: >-
  Cross-language runtime benchmark covering 19 programming languages
  (C, C++, Rust, Zig, Go, Nim, Fortran, Ada, D, Java, C#, OCaml, Dart,
  Pascal, JS Bun/Node, PHP, CPython, PyPy3) on five workloads: trial
  division primes, recursive Fibonacci, string equality, Mandelbrot, and
  binary trees. Records per-workload wall time, process CPU time, peak RSS
  and native binary size, and verifies identical checksums across languages.
  Toolchains pinned via Nix flake for reproducibility.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - programming-languages
  - performance
  - language-comparison
  - reproducible-benchmarks
license: MIT
version: "2026.09"
date-released: "2026-09-03"
